{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-php-1-intro","title":"Philippians 1 — Chapter Introduction","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PHP","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":0,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":0},"content":"<p>let. 25,28,29; Col 3:19; 1Pe 3:7 reverence. 22; 1Ki 1:31; Es 1:20; Heb 12:9; 1Pe 3:2-6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-php-1-1","title":"Philippians 1:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PHP","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Paul testifies his thankfulness to God, and his love towards them, for the fruits of their faith, and fellowship in his sufferings; 9 daily praying to him for their increase in grace; 12 he shows what good the faith of Christ had received by his troubles at Rome; 21 and how ready he is to glorify Christ either by his life or death; 27 exhorting them to unity; 28 and to fortitude in persecution.</p>\n<p>Paul. Ro 1:1; 1Co 1:1 Timotheus. Ac 16:1-3; 1Co 16:10; 2Co 1:1; Col 1:1; 1Th 1:1; 2Th 1:1; 1Ti 1:2 Heb 13:23 the servants. Mr 13:34; Joh 12:26; Tit 1:1; Jas 1:1; 2Pe 1:1; Jude 1:1 Re 1:1; 19:10; 22:9 the saints. Ro 1:7; 1Co 1:2; 2Co 1:1; Eph 1:1,15; 2Th 1:10 Philippi. Ac 16:12-15; 1Th 2:2 the bishops. Ac 1:20; 1Ti 3:1,2; Tit 1:7; 1Pe 2:25; Re 1:20; 2:1,8,12 and deacons. Ac 6:1-7; 1Ti 3:8,10,12,13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-php-1-2","title":"Philippians 1:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PHP","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>Ro 1:7; 2Co 1:2; 1Pe 1:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-php-1-3","title":"Philippians 1:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PHP","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>I thank. Ro 1:8,9; 6:17; 1Co 1:4 upon. Eph 1:15,16; Col 1:3,4; 1Th 1:2,3; 3:9; 2Th 1:3; 2Ti 1:3; Phm 1:4,5 remembrance. or, mention.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-php-1-4","title":"Philippians 1:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PHP","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":4},